tools.description:
Search the user's recipe library. Returns CSV with a `link` column — copy a `[title](/recipes/{id})` cell verbatim into `get_recipe`.

WHERE clause examples:
  Equality:       {"cuisines":"italian"}
  Array member:   {"tags":{"contains":"vegetarian"}}
  Any-of:         {"tags":{"contains_any":["vegetarian","vegan"]}}
  Comparison:     {"cook_time_minutes":{"lte":30}}
  AND (implicit): {"cuisines":"italian","cook_time_minutes":{"lte":30}}
  OR:             {"or":[{"cuisines":"italian"},{"cuisines":"mexican"}]}
  NOT:            {"not":{"tags":{"contains":"dessert"}}}
  Title search:   {"title":{"contains":"lasagna"}}
  Nutrition:      {"nutrition_calories":{"lte":400}}, {"nutrition_protein_g":{"gte":30}}

Operators: eq, gt, gte, lt, lte (comparison); contains, contains_any, contains_all (arrays); and, or, not (logical).
IMPORTANT: All indexed values including titles are normalized to English, lowercase, singular. Use "chicken" not "Chicken", "pancake" not "Pannkakor".
get_recipe_stats helps discover available filter values.
Omit where entirely to list all recipes.
Note: recently saved recipes may take a moment to appear in search results.

